# Frontend Build & Asset Rules

- Root NPM scripts:
  - `build:js`/`watch:js` invoke Gulp tasks; see [`gulpfile.js`](mdc:gulpfile.js).
  - `build:ckeditor` uses Webpack; see [`webpack.config.js`](mdc:webpack.config.js) and sources in [`js-src/ckeditor5-build-classic`](mdc:js-src/ckeditor5-build-classic).
  - `build:css`/`watch:css` use Brunch; sources are under [`cp-styles/app`](mdc:cp-styles/app), outputs to `themes/ee`.
- Additional package.json files exist in [`frontedit`](mdc:frontedit) and [`build-tools`](mdc:build-tools). Check local `gulpfile.js`/`vue.config.js` as needed.

## Conventions

- Prefer TypeScript in `cp-styles/app/main.ts` and related modules; keep strict types.
- Match existing module patterns in `themes/ee/*` when updating shipped assets.
- Avoid introducing new build tools; extend Gulp/Brunch/Webpack configs instead.
- When editing styles, keep variables/mixins centralized and avoid inline styles.